[125.200918, "o", "exec(open('train_lora.py').read().split('def main():')[0].replace('import json\\nimport os',''))\r\ntok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(BASE_MODEL)\r\ntok.pad_token = tok.eos_token\r\ndata = json.load(open('/app/data/train.json'))\r\nprompts = [format_prompt(s) for s in data[:3]]\r\nenc = tok(prompts, add_special_tokens=False, padding='max_length', truncation=True, max_length=MAX_LEN, return_tensors='pt')\r\nlabels = enc['input_ids'].clone()\r\nprefix_ids = tok.encode('Answer: ', add_special_tokens=False)\r\npl = len(prefix_ids)\r\nfor i in range(3):\r\n    row = labels[i]\r\n    non_pad = (row != tok.pad_token_id).nonzero().flatten()\r\n    start, end = non_pad[0].item(), non_pad[-1].item()\r\n    mask = torch.zeros_like(row, dtype=torch.bool)\r\n    mask[start+pl:end+1] = True\r\n    print('unmasked:', [tok.decode([t]) for t in row[mask].tolist()], 'expected:', data[i]['answer'])\r\nEOF — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && python - <<'EOF' import json, torch from transformers impor…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 14 tool call"]
[125.200952, "o", "(s) so far\r\n  [tools] Stopped: the same tool call repeated 3 times without progress, after 14 call(s).\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — wrapping up\r\n  [endpoint] qwen3.8-27b refused a system message after the first — resending gnomon's own messages as user messages marked [gnomon], for the rest of this session. Declare steer_role = \"user\" on the endpoint to skip the refused call.\r\n  qwen3.8-27b\r\nThe label-masking check kept printing the whole prompt instead of just the answer token, so I could not confirm the mask is correct — and I have not run the training yet, so none of the required outputs exist on disk yet.\r\n\r\nWhat I did complete:\r\n- Installed torch (CPU), peft==0.15.0, transformers, datasets, accelerate.\r\n- Wrote /app/train_lora.py (GPT-2 + LoRA r=8, alpha=16, target c_attn, 3 epochs, batch 8, lr 1e-4, saves adapter to /app/experiments/lora_adapter and /app/lora_results.json).\r\n\r\nWhat is unverified / not done:\r\n- The mask logic in train_lora.py is suspect: my check printed the entire prompt as \"unmasked\", which "]
[125.201026, "o", "means either the mask is wrong or my check was wrong. I could not tell which.\r\n- Training has not been run; /app/experiments/lora_adapter and /app/lora_results.json do not exist yet.\r\n- No accuracy check has been performed.\r\n\r\nTo finish: fix/verify the label mask (only the answer-letter token should be supervised), run `python /app/train_lora.py`, then load the adapter and evaluate on val.json to sanity-check before the held-out test.\r\n\r\n_[Stopped: the same tool call repeated 3 times without progress, after 14 call(s).]_\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-27b tools=14 surface=9a6bfc32cece\r\n"]
